<title>GERMANY: German metals imports down in 1996 as demand eases.</title>
<headline>German metals imports down in 1996 as demand eases.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German metals industry data issued on Tuesday showed weaker domestic demand in 1996 weighed on the imports of semi-fabricated and finished metals while more finished metals were exported.</p>
<p>The metals industry association WVM at its annual news conference gave trade details for 1996 in semis and in base metals as follows in '000 tonnes. Columns may not add up exactly due to rounding --</p>
<p>				  1996		1995	pct change</p>
<p>									  96/95</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p>    Semis		     924		 1,087	  - 15.0</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>	aluminium		   502		 594	- 15.5</p>
<p>	copper			350		 417	- 16.1</p>
<p>	lead			    6		   6	   0.0</p>
<p>	zinc			   56		  60	-  6.3</p>
<p>	others			 10		  10	   0.0</p>
<p>     Metals		  2,066		 2,402	  - 14.0</p>
<p> of which</p>
<p>	aluminium		 1,066	     1,316	- 19.0</p>
<p>	copper			605		 650	-  7.0</p>
<p>	lead			  154		 145	+  6.0</p>
<p>	zinc			  242		 291	- 17.0</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>    Semis		   1,356		 1,427	  -  5.0</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>	aluminium		   673		 701	-  4.0</p>
<p>	copper			612		 656	-  6.7</p>
<p>	lead			   17		  18	-  7.7</p>
<p>	zinc			   34		  34	   0.0</p>
<p>	others			 21		  18	+ 15.4</p>
<p>    Metals		    586		   553	  +  6.0</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>	aluminium		   250		 263	-  4.9</p>
<p>	copper			213		 158	+ 35.0</p>
<p>	lead			   35		  43	- 19.4</p>
<p>	zinc			   88		  89	-  1.4</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Duesseldorf newsroom, +49-211-3882244</p>
